<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Luxembourg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Luxembourg was a dynasty of counts of Luxembourg that rose to the first rank of European royalty in the fourteenth century. It produced the emperors Henry VII, Charles IV and Sigismund, ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> from 1310 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> from 1387, and held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> from 1373. The male line ended with Sigismund in 1437, and most of its lands passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-luxembourg.jpg" alt="House of Luxembourg" width="320" height="391" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wereszczyński · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:COA_Luxembourg_with_crest.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
